# Buytly Server

Follow `.cursor/rules/docs-sync.mdc` — update docs in the same PR as code changes.

Key references in `server/docs/`:

- `architecture.md` — layers and request lifecycle
- `api-rules.md` — response shape, pagination, rate limits
- `modules.md` — endpoint contracts
- `database-schema.md` — collections and indexes
- `auth-flow.md` — JWT lifecycle and auth flows
- `roles.md` — role definitions, permissions, and authorization layers
- `deployment.md` — env vars and production setup

## Module pattern

Each domain module under `server/src/modules/<name>/`:

- `*.routes.js` — routes, Swagger annotations, middleware chain
- `*.controller.js` — thin HTTP handlers (delegate to service)
- `*.service.js` — business logic, DB, external services
- `*.model.js` — Mongoose schema (when persisted)
- `*.validation.js` — Zod schemas

Routes: `router → validate → authenticate/authorize → asyncHandler(controller)`.

## Conventions

- Use `ApiResponse.success` / `ApiResponse.paginated` / `ApiResponse.created` for all responses
- Throw `AppError` from services; never send raw `res.status()` from services
- Validate with Zod via `validate()` / `validateMultiple()` middleware
- Cross-cutting concerns: `server/src/services/` (email, GCS, cache, tokens)
- Notifications: call `notificationService.notify()` — never email from controllers
- Listing detail reads use `buildProjectReadFilter` / `buildPropertyReadFilter` (anyone sees non-trashed docs; status checks then hide drafts); writes keep `buildProjectIdFilter` / `buildPropertyIdFilter` (owner/agent or admin only)
- Listing prices can be hidden per site (`features.hidePublicPrices`): any read path that returns unit `price` or project `priceMin`/`priceMax` to non-managers must go through `src/shared/priceVisibility.js` (`hideUnitPrice` / `hideProjectPriceRange`); see `docs/api-rules.md` "Hidden prices"
- Email links and branding are per site: build frontend URLs with `buildSiteLink(path)` (`services/siteBrand.js`), not `env.APP_URL` (fallback only), and never hard-code "Buytly" in email copy — templates get `brand.name`
- Scripts that write tenant data (`server/scripts/`, e.g. `seed/block57.js`) run inside `runWithRequestContext({ site })` and call the module services rather than raw model writes, so validation, status rules, notifications and branding match the API; production bootstraps must be safe to re-run
- New endpoints: update `server/docs/modules.md`, add Swagger annotations (paths relative to `/api/v1`, e.g. `/properties` not `/api/v1/properties`)
- Swagger: define reusable schemas in `server/src/config/swagger.schemas.js`; each operation needs `operationId`, request/response `$ref`s, and standard error responses (for Orval)

## Tests

- Run from `server/`: `npm test`
- Unit tests for Zod schemas; integration tests use Vitest + Supertest (require MongoDB on `buytly-test` DB or set `MONGODB_URI`)
- Set env in `tests/setup.js`; do not import `src/` before test env is configured
